Z||000000||deceler8||10-17-2001||07:59 AM||||I'm so pissed...car wash vacuum snagged my passenger seat and ripped it. Seat WAS perfect...<P>What I'm wondering is what, if any, seats fit without any mods...I know F body seats fit, but I'm 6'2 and sit pretty close to the roof as it is.<P>And all I'm looking for is a basic set of buckets. Has anyone used anything like Cavalier or Grand Am buckets, and if so, how do they fit ? I don't want to lose headroom.<P>Are most GM compact buckets the same, and can the Fiero tracks be used on most of them ?<P>I know there are lots of posts on this topic, but wondered if anyone has done this recently.<P>All of this assumes I can't find a grey Fiero pass. seat at the wreckers, or a suitable grey seatback cover. Honestly, I haven't looked yet.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/deceler8_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-17-2001||08:10 AM||||A nice used grey seat cover is a lot less expensive that replacement seats.  Put in a request in the mall section.  I replaced my drivers seat cover with a passenger seat cover I bought from George/Terry in California.||||reg||1
